  "description": "Trap (formula re-audit NEW-4, LOW: Table 4 presentation in mixed-sign heads). Karnataka client; every document is CGST + SGST, so all four buckets share one head. (1) SS/3301 Sunrise Steel raw material, taxable 1,00,000, 9,000 + 9,000, matched in GSTR-2B (forward, not blocked). (2) HM/CN/205 Horizon Motors credit note on the director's car bought in August (s.17(5) motor vehicle), taxable 50,000, 4,500 + 4,500, in GSTR-2B CDNR (forward, blocked: -4,500 / -4,500). (3) KD/CN/19 Adv. Kavita Deshmukh & Associates (unregistered, legal services, reverse charge Yes) credit note on the September retainer, taxable 50,000, no tax in the books -> 18% -> -4,500 / -4,500 (reverse charge, not blocked). (4) RTT/88 Ravi Tours and Travels (unregistered), 'Directors Cab Hire' (s.17(5) rent-a-cab), reverse charge Yes, taxable 3,60,000 at 5%, 9,000 + 9,000 in the books (reverse charge, blocked). Hand working: outward 5,00,000 -> 45,000 + 45,000 (90,000). 3.1(d) = 9,000 - 4,500 = 4,500 per head (rcmTaxPaise 9,000; rcmTaxablePaise 3,60,000 - 50,000 = 3,10,000); no 3.1(d) excess. Table 4 buckets, never netted against each other: 4(A)(5) = 9,000 (not blocked) + 0 (blocked bucket -4,500 is negative) = 9,000 per head; 4(A)(3) = 0 (not blocked bucket -4,500 is negative) + 9,000 (blocked) = 9,000 per head; available 36,000. 4(B)(1) = 0 + 9,000 = 9,000 per head (18,000): the blocked car note reverses in 4(B)(1)'s bucket, not 4(B)(2). Blocked-note excess 4,500 per head (9,000), kept out of 4(A)(5). The negative not-blocked reverse-charge bucket (N = 4,500 per head) is not netted against the blocked cab ITC; a credit note reduces the liability and the matching ITC in the same period, and 3.1(d) already netted the legal note (signed total L = +4,500, no 3.1(d) excess), so the ITC side carries min(N, neg0(L)) = 0 and the 4,500 per head is reversed now in 4(B)(2) (owner decision: conservative drafts). 4(B)(2) 4,500 per head (itcOtherReversalPaise 9,000); a3 carry-forward nil. Net ITC 4(C) = 9,000 + 9,000 - 9,000 - 4,500 = 4,500 per head (9,000). Set-off: credit 4,500 per head -> cash 40,500 + 4,500 RCM = 45,000 per head (90,000); credit used 9,000; closing credit 0. No expected filing date: 0 days late, no interest, no late fee. Warn flag: gst.blocked-credit (RTT/88); gst.negative-rcm passes (nothing carried on either side). The old code netted the buckets: 4(A)(3) 4,500, 4(A)(5) 4,500, 4(B)(1) 4,500, 4(B)(2) nil per head (available 18,000, blocked 9,000), no excess; net 9,000 and cash 90,000 as now.",
